 "text": "Hey! How's everything going? Of course. You want a long cooked pasta noodle so it's barely there, or a bagel slice with a hummus dip sandwich? Celiac is a real thing, and there's a lot of great advice online about gluten free food. The key is what feels like real bread. Oatmeal pies, oat cakes, even some rice crackers or couscous salads are usually fine. Soy sauce is generally fine, just check the label. If it says it' made with barley or another gluten grain, it's not safe. Sushi is usually safe, as long as it' not made with any of the common problem ingredients.",
